{"id":30939687135,"name":"Run api tests","node_id":"WFR_kwLOA_1uaM8AAAAHNCYo3w","head_branch":"claude/uganda-18-parallel-pi-fanout","head_sha":"a2565f33761efd950d4204f0a9ee2cc05bed424f","path":".github/workflows/run-api-tests.yml","run_number":51736,"run_attempt":1,"event":"pull_request","display_title":"perf: run the planned event/program-indicator queries concurrently","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","workflow_id":5591308,"check_suite_id":83906739895,"check_suite_node_id":"CS_kwDOA_1uaM8AAAATiTs-tw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30939687135","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30939687135","created_at":"2026-08-04T18:40:02Z","updated_at":"2026-08-04T18:56:30Z","run_started_at":"2026-08-04T18:40:02Z","jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30939687135/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30939687135/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/check-suites/83906739895","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30939687135/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30939687135/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30939687135/rerun","head_commit":{"message":"perf: run the planned event/program-indicator queries concurrently\n\nAn aggregate analytics request carrying 200 dx items, 70 of them program\nindicators, executed 81 statements against analytics_event_uebhwkwll5v one after\nanother: 0.23-0.32 s each, a flat ~12 entries/second for 21 consecutive seconds,\n95.6% of the request's JDBC time. Nothing overlapped. The 130 non-PI items were\nserved by 8 queries in 0.279 s - about 271 ms per program indicator against 2.1 ms\nper everything else.\n\nThe asymmetry was in the code, not the data. The aggregate data-value path is\n@Async and returns a Future, awaited by DataHandler.executeQueries. The event and\nprogram-indicator path was a plain for loop over a blocking call in\nEventAggregateService.addData, and the trace's auxThreadStats shows 4 ms of CPU on\na second thread: there was another thread and it did nothing.\n\nEach planned query now fills a grid of its own and the partial grids are appended\nin the planner's order, so no two threads write to one grid and the result is\nunchanged row for row. The target grid's headers are copied into each partial grid\nbecause PiDisagDataHandler resolves the data dimension by header index.\n\nConcurrency deliberately does not use Spring's @Async executor. With no\nTaskExecutor bean configured, @EnableAsync falls back to SimpleAsyncTaskExecutor,\nwhich starts a thread per task and bounds nothing; the data-value path survives that\nonly because its planner has already collapsed the work into at most 8 groups. This\nfan-out is one query per program indicator per partition and is not bounded in\nadvance, so EventQueryExecutor caps it at databaseServerCpus (or the core count),\nnever above 8, and queues the rest rather than rejecting it.\n\nMeasured with 81 real Postgres queries over a Hikari pool, ~78 ms each, three\npasses, before = the serial loop this replaces:\n\n  cap=1   6542 -\u003e 6472 ms   1.0x\n  cap=2   6206 -\u003e 3163 ms   2.0x\n  cap=4   6357 -\u003e 3146 ms   2.0x\n  cap=8   6444 -\u003e 3442 ms   1.9x\n\nTwo things to read off that. It is ~2x, not cap-x: the database saturates, which is\nexactly the risk this change carries and the reason for the cap. And the first\nversion of this was 7% SLOWER than the loop at cap=1, because it handed every task\nto a single worker and blocked - hence the single-threaded configuration now runs on\nthe calling thread, with a test pinning it.\n\nUganda's own speed-up is not this number. Their database server is not this\ncontainer, and their per-query cost is a correlated subquery fan-out rather than the\nsequential scan used here.\n\nRefs UGANDA-18, UGANDA-10 finding F10.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","author":{"name":"stian-sandvold","email":"stian@dhis2.org"},"id":"a2565f33761efd950d4204f0a9ee2cc05bed424f","tree_id":"0fbc47e69e1a4604bc60c2132f1c8a7754a9b678","timestamp":"2026-08-04T15:42:31Z","committer":{"name":"stian-sandvold","email":"stian@dhis2.org"}},"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/workflows/5591308","repository":{"id":66940520,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk2Njk0MDUyMA==","owner":{"login":"dhis2","id":1089987,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjEwODk5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1089987?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2","gravatar_id":"","type":"Organization","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/subscriptions"},"name":"dhis2-core","full_name":"dhis2/dhis2-core","description":"DHIS 2 Core. Written in Java. Contains the service layer and Web API.","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2/dhis2-core","fork":false,"private":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/{archive_format}{/ref}","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/assignees{/user}","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/git/blobs{/sha}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/branches{/branch}","c